  <data name="Vm_WhatsNewHeading" xml:space="preserve"><value>What's new in Portal AI Host {0}</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn1Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Thank you</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn1Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Thank you for your feedback and reports. They shaped this update.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn2Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>The tray pop-up no longer crashes</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn2Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>The small status window from the tray icon could crash the first time it opened. That is fixed.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn3Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Removing a device stops it at once</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn3Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>When you remove a device, anything it was still asking for now stops straight away.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn4Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pairing a new PC is safer</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn4Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>A laptop paired with a new home PC no longer risks sending the old PC's access token to it.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn5Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use your home PC from a laptop</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn5Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pair a laptop with your home PC once. Apps on the laptop then use the home PC's AI, at home or away, and fall back to the laptop's own model if you choose.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn6Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Devices on this PC</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn6Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>See each paired laptop on its own card. Pause it, set daily limits and quiet hours, choose which models it may use, or take back a model it loaded.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn7Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Two models at once</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn7Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>A laptop you trust can keep a second model loaded on your PC, for example one on the graphics card and one in memory. Your own model is never pushed out.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn8Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Gaming mode works in windowed games</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn8Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Turn on gaming mode and other devices are told your PC is busy while a game runs, including games in a window.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn9Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Relay access key</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn9Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Only devices paired with your key can reach this PC away from home. Make a new key at any time.</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn10Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>See your memory at a glance</value></data>
  <data name="Vm_Wn10Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>Bars on the Models page show how much memory and graphics memory the loaded models use, against your limits.</value></data>
